  "title": { "en": "Numbers 11–20 and sound review", "es": "Del once al veinte y repaso" },
  "objectives": [
    "Count from 11 to 20",
    "Spell 16–19 and 21–29 correctly, with the right accents",
    "Understand prices up to 20 euros",
    "Review every Level 1 sound before the checkpoint"
  ],
  "teach": [
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "once, doce, trece, catorce, quince", "en": "11, 12, 13, 14, 15", "note": "Five one-off words, and every one has a θ: ON-θe, DO-θe, TRE-θe, ka-TOR-θe, KIN-θe." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "dieciséis, diecisiete, dieciocho, diecinueve, veinte", "en": "16, 17, 18, 19, 20" },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**16–19 are 'ten and six', squeezed into one word:** diez y seis → **dieciséis**.\n\n- The z of **diez** turns into c before i (the day 4 spelling rule): **dieci-**.\n- **dieciséis** needs an accent. It ends in s and is stressed on the last syllable, which breaks rule 1 from day 2. The others follow the rules: diecisiete, dieciocho, diecinueve."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**21–29 work the same way**, from **veinte**: veinti + number, as one word.\n\n- With an accent: **veintidós, veintitrés, veintiséis** (they end in s and are stressed on the last syllable).\n- Without one: veintiuno, veinticuatro, veinticinco, veintisiete, veintiocho, veintinueve.\n- Before a masculine noun, veintiuno becomes **veintiún**: veintiún euros.\n\nFrom 31 on it's three words: **treinta y uno**."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Level 1 sound checklist**\n\n- Five pure vowels: a e i o u\n- Stress and written accents: papa / papá\n- Silent h; soft d in nada\n- θ for z/ce/ci, s for s: casa / caza\n- Strong j for j/ge/gi; hard and soft g: gato, amigo\n- Tap r and trilled rr: pero / perro\n- ñ in España\n- ll = y; b = v; ch as in church"
    }
  ],
  "vocab": [
